.TH GERANT 1 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
gerant \- start, stop and list garnish VMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gerant start
.I name
.br
.B gerant stop
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.I name
.br
.B gerant list
.br
.B gerant ssh
.I name
.RI [ command ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gerant
is the command line client of
.BR gerantd (1),
which runs the crosvm virtual machines configured in
.IR ~/.config/garnish/vms/ .
It talks to
.B gerantd
over the session bus; the first call starts it through D-Bus activation.
.PP
A VM's name is the name of its configuration file without
.IR .conf ;
see
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI start " name"
Start the VM and return once crosvm runs, while the guest is still booting.
Prints the VM's vsock CID, its addresses (with
.BR Mode=nat ),
its log directory and how to reach it with
.BR ssh .
If the start fails, the error has the end of crosvm's log.
.TP
.BR stop " [" \-\-force ]
.I name
Press the VM's ACPI power button, so the guest shuts down cleanly, and wait
until the VM is off. If the guest is still up after
.B StopTimeoutSec=
(see
.BR gerantd.conf (5)),
.B gerantd
stops crosvm.
With
.BR \-\-force ,
stop crosvm right away without asking the guest.
.TP
.B list
List every configured VM with its state
.RB ( stopped ,
.BR starting ,
.BR booting ,
.B running
or
.BR stopping )
and, for running ones, the CID, IPv4 address, tap device and IPv6 address.
.TP
.BI ssh " name" " \fR[\fPcommand\fR ...]\fP"
Run
.BI "ssh " user @vsock/ cid
for a running VM, with
.I command
if given. The host name
.BI vsock/ cid
needs systemd's ssh proxy (systemd 256 or newer).
.I user
is the VM's
.B [Guest] User=
setting.
.IP
The guest's host key is checked against the VM's name, not its CID, since
CIDs are reused by other VMs, including other users'.
The first connection records the key in
.IR ~/.local/state/garnish/known_hosts ;
if it changes later, for example after rebuilding the image, ssh refuses to
connect until the old key is removed with
.BI "ssh\-keygen \-R " name " \-f ~/.local/state/garnish/known_hosts" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/garnish/vms/name.conf
The VM's configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/garnish/name/
The VM's logs, starting with
.IR console.log ,
the guest's serial console.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/garnish/known_hosts
The guests' ssh host keys, by VM name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ mkdir \-p ~/.config/garnish/vms
$ cp /usr/share/doc/gerant/examples/debian.conf ~/.config/garnish/vms/
$ gerant start debian
$ gerant ssh debian uname \-a
$ gerant stop debian
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gerantd (1),
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5),
.BR salle (1),
.BR garnish (7)
